# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and adjust. Vite reads these at start-up.

# Base URL of the metamorph API. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Set to "true" to show the username-only dev login in a production build.
# It is always shown under `vite dev`.
VITE_DEV_LOGIN=false

# The desktop app (Tauri on Linux, macOS, Windows) cannot use Google's web button (its webview blocks the pop-up), so
# it signs in through the system browser. Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" in Google Cloud Console and
# put its id and secret in app/.env.local for `pnpm tauri dev`, or app/.env.desktop.local for a release build (both are
# git-ignored); the secret of a desktop client is not confidential, but it still stays out of git. The API must list the
# desktop client id in GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS (comma-separated).
# VITE_GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=
# VITE_GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# OAuth 2.0 Web client ID from Google Cloud Console (Credentials), with this
# app's origin listed under "Authorized JavaScript origins". When unset, the
# "Continue with Google" button is not rendered and Google's script is not loaded.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Android only: the id of an OAuth client of type "Android" (package com.smarniw.metamorph, "Enable custom URI scheme"
# on) for the browser sign-in that phones without Google Play services use. It is set in .env.android. The API must
# list it in GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS.
# VITE_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
